        "kind": "url"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "line": 45,
      "section": "main",
      "depth": 0,
      "text": "Part 1: building blocks of distributed communication/computation",
      "extra": {
        "level": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "section_start",
      "line": 75,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 76,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "**Collective operations** are the conceptual primitives used for distributed programming",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "cite",
      "line": 76,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Collective_operation",
      "extra": {
        "kind": "url",
        "via": "article_link"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 77,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "- These are classic in the parallel programming literature from the 1980s.",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 78,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "- *Collective* means that you specify a general communication pattern across many devices.",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 79,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "- This can be better/faster than managing point-to-point communication yourself.",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 81,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "**Setup**:",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "figure",
      "line": 82,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "images/ranks.png",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 83,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "- **Rank**: a particular device/GPU (e.g., 0, 1, 2, 3)",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 84,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "- **World size**: total number of devices (e.g., 4)",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 86,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "Operations:",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 87,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "- Broadcast, scatter, gather, reduce (foundations)",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 88,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "- All-gather, reduce-scatter, all-reduce (workhorse)",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 89,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "- All-to-all (for MoEs)",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 91,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "**Broadcast**: copy from rank 0 to all ranks",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "line": 93,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "rank0 = tensor([0., 1, 2, 3])\nrank0 = tensor([0., 1, 2, 3])\nrank1 = tensor([0., 1, 2, 3])\nrank2 = tensor([0., 1, 2, 3])\nrank3 = tensor([0., 1, 2, 3])",
      "extra": {
        "end_line": 99
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 101,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "Minor use case: rank 0 loads initial checkpoint and broadcasts to all ranks",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 103,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "**Scatter** tensor on rank 0 to all ranks",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "line": 105,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "rank0 = tensor([0., 1, 2, 3])\nrank0 = tensor([0.])\nrank1 = tensor([1.])\nrank2 = tensor([2.])\nrank3 = tensor([3.])",
      "extra": {
        "end_line": 111
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 113,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "Note: stepping stone to understanding reduce-scatter",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 115,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "**Gather** pieces from all ranks to rank 0 (opposite of scatter)",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "line": 117,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "rank0 = tensor([0.])\nrank1 = tensor([1.])\nrank2 = tensor([2.])\nrank3 = tensor([3.])\nrank0 = tensor([0., 1, 2, 3])",
      "extra": {
        "end_line": 123
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 125,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "Note: stepping stone to understanding all-gather",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 127,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "**Reduce** pieces from all ranks to rank 0, applying some operation (e.g., sum, min, max)",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "line": 129,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "rank0 = tensor([0.])\nrank1 = tensor([1.])\nrank2 = tensor([2.])\nrank3 = tensor([3.])\nrank0 = tensor([6.])  # Sum of all ranks (0 + 1 + 2 + 3)",
      "extra": {
        "end_line": 135
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 137,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "Note: stepping stone to understanding all-reduce",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 139,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "**All-gather**: perform gather to all ranks, not just rank 0",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "line": 141,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "rank0 = tensor([0.])\nrank1 = tensor([1.])\nrank2 = tensor([2.])\nrank3 = tensor([3.])\nrank0 = tensor([0., 1, 2, 3])\nrank1 = tensor([0., 1, 2, 3])\nrank2 = tensor([0., 1, 2, 3])\nrank3 = tensor([0., 1, 2, 3])",
      "extra": {
        "end_line": 150
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 152,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "Use case: each rank holds parameter shard, gather to get full parameters for forward pass",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 154,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "**Reduce-scatter**: perform reduce on each dimension, scatter results",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "line": 156,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "rank0 = tensor([0., 1, 2, 3])\nrank1 = tensor([1., 2, 3, 4])\nrank2 = tensor([2., 3, 4, 5])\nrank3 = tensor([3., 4, 5, 6])\nrank0 = tensor([6.])  # Sum along dim 0 (0 + 1 + 2 + 3)\nrank1 = tensor([10.]) # Sum along dim 1 (1 + 2 + 3 + 4)\nrank2 = tensor([14.]) # Sum along dim 2 (2 + 3 + 4 + 5)\nrank3 = tensor([18.]) # Sum along dim 3 (3 + 4 + 5 + 6)",
      "extra": {
        "end_line": 165
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 167,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "Use case: after backward pass, sum gradients from different data shards, but distribute storage",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 169,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "**All-reduce** = reduce-scatter + all-gather",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "line": 171,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "rank0 = tensor([0., 1, 2, 3])\nrank1 = tensor([1., 2, 3, 4])\nrank2 = tensor([2., 3, 4, 5])\nrank3 = tensor([3., 4, 5, 6])\nrank0 = tensor([6., 10, 14, 18])\nrank1 = tensor([6., 10, 14, 18])\nrank2 = tensor([6., 10, 14, 18])\nrank3 = tensor([6., 10, 14, 18])",
      "extra": {
        "end_line": 180
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 182,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "Use case: after backward pass, sum gradients from different data shards, but replicate full parameters",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 183,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "Breaking all-reduce into reduce-scatter + all-gather allows for flexibility (e.g., ZeRO/FSDP)",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 185,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "**All-to-all**: each rank sends each other rank some tensor (most general)",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "line": 187,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "rank0 = tensor([0., 1, 2, 3])      # send  0 to rank 0,  1 to rank 1,  2 to rank 2,  3 to rank 3\nrank1 = tensor([4., 5, 6, 7])      # send  4 to rank 0,  5 to rank 1,  6 to rank 2,  7 to rank 3\nrank2 = tensor([8., 9, 10, 11])    # send  8 to rank 0,  9 to rank 1, 10 to rank 2, 11 to rank 3\nrank3 = tensor([12., 13, 14, 15])  # send 12 to rank 0, 13 to rank 1, 14 to rank 2, 15 to rank 3\nrank0 = tensor([0, 4, 8, 12])\nrank1 = tensor([1, 5, 9, 13])\nrank2 = tensor([2, 6, 10, 14])\nrank3 = tensor([3, 7, 11, 15])",
      "extra": {
        "end_line": 196
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 198,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "Notes:",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 199,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "- Useful for MoEs: each rank has split of data and subset of experts; need to route data to experts",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 200,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "- For balanced splits, all-to-all looks like transpose",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 201,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "- Also handles unbalanced splits (but want splits to be as balanced as possible)",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 203,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "Way to remember the terminology:",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 204,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "- Reduce: performs some associative/commutative operation (sum, min, max)",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 205,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "- Scatter is inverse of gather",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "line": 206,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "- All: means destination is all devices",
      "extra": {}
    },
    {
      "kind": "section_end",
      "line": 206,
      "section": "collective_operations",
      "depth": 1,
      "text": "",
      "extra": {}
    },
